From: AdrielOrihuela <adriel.orihuela.m@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 31 Oct 2026 01:05:58 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] Read spigot.yml from memory when it is built from the TOML
 files

SpigotConfig loads its file, reads every value with its own default and
saves the result back. With spigot.yml built in memory from the TOML
files there is no file to load and none to save: init(YamlConfiguration)
takes the built configuration as it is, and readConfig skips the save
when there is no file, where save(null) would throw.

Everything after the load is unchanged, so SpigotConfig and every
SpigotWorldConfig read the values exactly as before, and
Bukkit.spigot().getConfig() returns the same object.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>

diff --git a/src/main/java/org/spigotmc/SpigotConfig.java b/src/main/java/org/spigotmc/SpigotConfig.java
index 78fd32976b9394d5a6ddeb0444eae3f5703ab940..24b9313c4b331935157cc58184b98ebe5673b6f4 100644
--- a/src/main/java/org/spigotmc/SpigotConfig.java
+++ b/src/main/java/org/spigotmc/SpigotConfig.java
@@ -62,6 +62,22 @@ public class SpigotConfig {
             throw Throwables.propagate(ex);
         }
 
+        SpigotConfig.readLoaded();
+    }
+
+    // LegacyFolia start - spigot.yml is built in memory from the TOML files
+    /**
+     * Reads a configuration built in memory, with no file behind it: nothing is loaded and
+     * nothing is saved. {@code Bukkit.spigot().getConfig()} returns this same object.
+     */
+    public static void init(YamlConfiguration built) {
+        SpigotConfig.CONFIG_FILE = null;
+        SpigotConfig.config = built;
+        SpigotConfig.readLoaded();
+    }
+
+    static void readLoaded() { // not private: readConfig calls every private method that takes nothing
+        // LegacyFolia end - spigot.yml is built in memory from the TOML files
         SpigotConfig.config.options().header(SpigotConfig.HEADER);
         SpigotConfig.config.options().copyDefaults(true);
 
@@ -95,6 +111,7 @@ public class SpigotConfig {
             }
         }
 
+        if (SpigotConfig.CONFIG_FILE == null) return; // LegacyFolia - built in memory, there is no file to save
         try {
             SpigotConfig.config.save(SpigotConfig.CONFIG_FILE);
         } catch (IOException ex) {
